s a living instrument panel\u2014not a flat utility sheet. Read the time and date, watch battery level rise and fall, and see pack heat and headset thermal stress at a glance, rendered as brass-and-copper machinery you can anchor on a wall. The background mood shifts with the hour\u2014from dawn light to evening dusk.\n\nFeatures:\n\u2022 Stereoscopic copper infinity-cube sculpture with spatial depth\n\u2022 Steam-era clock and calendar displays\n\u2022 Background mood that changes with the time of day\n\u2022 Battery level with charging indication\n\u2022 Battery temperature thermometer with warning glow when hot\n\u2022 Headset thermal-stress gauge with flashing warning lamp\n\u2022 Works 100% offline\n\u2022 No account needed, no data collected\n\nPerfect for Quest users who want a useful decorative piece in Passthrough or Immersive Home\u2014an ornamental wall sculpture and instrument in one window.\n\nNote: This is a lightweight 2D panel app that opens as a window in your Horizon OS home.", "short_description": "Windowed Home app that displays a sculptural copper infinity cube with spatial stereo depth, fitted with steam-era instruments for clock, date, battery level, pack temperature, and headset thermal status. Anchor the window to a wall in Passthrough or Immersive Home \u2014 a useful decorative piece for your space."}]}, "developer_name": null, "developer_privacy_policy_url": "https://gist.github.com/ravan1955/cc6b08a15a3a5b7cad37203943d12c09", "developer_terms_of_service_url": null, "publisher_name": "CodeWeaver", "support_website_url": null, "website_url": "https://ravan1955.github.io/Vernograph/", "category": null, "comfort_rating": "COMFORTABLE_FOR_MOST", "comfort_tags": [], "context_category": {"id": "362692211442873", "context_category": "APPS"}, "context_topics": [{"id": "393222478507326"}], "external_subscription_type": "NOT_REQUIRED", "genres": [], "has_in_app_ads": null, "internet_connection": "NOT_REQUIRED", "play_area": "NO_MOVEMENT", "recommen